WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.020
 Thank you very much. When I noticed at all, Senora C. Senores, I wanted to

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:11.000
 start with my language, Spanish.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:17.640
 I was born in Spain and grew up in Latin America. In any rate, good evening,

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.000
 ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:27.740
 First of all, allow me to congratulate and thank the handsome family for their

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:31.000
 awesome job that they perform every year,

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:37.400
 keeping alive the leadership of promoting and celebrating the leadership in our

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:40.000
 international communities.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:47.680
 Congratulations to all the individuals, wonderful leaders in this body,

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.000
 wonderful friends.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:56.320
 Today, I have the great honor to induct Carolyn Balogh to the International

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:59.000
 Hall of Fame.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:07.310
 Everyone in this audience, majority, knows Carolyn as a great leader, as a

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:10.000
 great businesswoman,

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:25.220
 CFO, HR director, and vice president of their own family business, Marva Ng.

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:28.000
 Also, a great leader in the Hawaiian community.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:38.280
 Tonight, in my short and brief remarks, only two minutes ago now, only a few of

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:41.000
 us, and I am one of the lucky ones,

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:50.000
 knew Carolyn's philanthropic role, vision, and support to the Spanish community.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:58.510
 I surprised Abby when I told her the story and I presented her fantasy. I knew

00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:01.000
 that she would be a winner.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:09.410
 I had the pleasure to meet Carolyn more than 20 years ago. We need to recognize

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:11.000
 time pass.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:20.470
 We were together serving at the El Barrio Board of Directors. We are one of the

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:27.000
 most successful Hispanic agencies in East North America.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:35.300
 She was, during those days, the first chair of the Programs Committee, and

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:44.000
 under her leadership, the job placement requests extended expectations.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:51.820
 She was able to develop a great partnership with company owners searching for

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:56.000
 employees to fill their job openings.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:05.000
 She also created a passing program for employees with transportation needs.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:12.210
 Additionally, Carolyn lived a girl, an after-school program at the elementary

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:17.000
 level, including mentoring and tutoring.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:24.000
 And all of this was done in the different locations of the school system.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:32.430
 Carolyn is well known for her professionalism, for her high emotional

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:42.000
 intelligence, and for her sensitivity and empathy toward others.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:52.200
 Her early education and empowering employees were two of her most notorious

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:57.000
 passions. Please welcome Carolyn Varo.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:22.000
 [BLANK_AUDIO]

